  "answer_text": "The link you provided\u2014`mvd.dor.ga.gov/tags/index.aspx`\u2014is an older, legacy web address for the **Georgia Department of Revenue (DOR) Motor Vehicle Division**. \n\nMost pages on the older `mvd.dor.ga.gov` domain have been updated and migrated to Georgia's modern digital portal. \n\n### Where to Go Instead:\nFor all tag, title, and vehicle registration services in Georgia, use the official, updated **Georgia DRIVES e-Services** portal:\n\n\ud83d\udc49 **[https://eservices.drives.ga.gov](https://eservices.drives.ga.gov)**\n\n---\n\n### What You Can Do on the Georgia DRIVES Portal:\n* **Renew Your Vehicle Registration (Tags):** Renew your annual registration online using your license plate number or VIN, along with your driver's license number or the Letter ID from your renewal notice.\n* **Look Up Specialty License Plate Designs:** Georgia offers hundreds of standard and specialty license plates (such as university, military, or special interest plates). You can search designs and estimate their costs.\n* **Estimate Title Ad Valorem Tax (TAVT):** Use the online calculator to estimate the TAVT owed on a newly purchased vehicle or a vehicle you are bringing into the state.\n* **Replace a License Plate or Decal:** Request a replacement if your current license plate, registration card, or decal is lost, damaged, or stolen.\n* **Cancel Registration Voluntarily:** If you sell your car, store it, or cancel your auto insurance, you can cancel your vehicle's registration online to prevent automatic fines.\n* **Find a Self-Service Kiosk:** Many counties in Georgia allow you to print your license plate decals instantly at participating grocery store kiosks (such as Kroger or Publix).\n\n*If you prefer to handle your vehicle tasks in person, you can search for your local [County Tag Office location](https://dor.georgia.gov/county-tag-offices).*",
